From a100e93585ee997c04933e88072987fa2dcfc570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:45:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: harden MLO association and metrics handling

Problem:

MLO association capabilities and link metrics could be lost or reported
inconsistently after link changes. Association-frame persistence was
also vulnerable to malformed data and concurrent updates, while the
11k response window was fixed at ten seconds.

Root cause:

Association frames were keyed only by an affiliated link and capability
reporting did not reliably verify frame availability. The association
frame database used unsynchronized read-modify-write operations and
exception-prone hexadecimal parsing. The 11k timeout was a compile-time
constant.

Fix:

Recover association capabilities using the client MLD and sibling AP MLD,
validate frame data, serialize and atomically persist database updates,
and make the 11k response timeout configurable. The existing MLO handling
and country-code advertisement changes from patch 0494 were already present
in the target history.

Change-Id: I7f4c1a8d2e6b4903a5c7d9e1f8b6c2a4d0e5f7b9
Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
